1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,400
MotionQA: evidence-backed PCB anomaly inspection.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,000
Team Kia Kiu, Institut Teknologi Bandung.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,600
Can you spot the defect on this benchmark board?

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:15,300
It is one bent pin: 262 pixels of
the model input, about 0.13 percent.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,200
A manual check records PASS or FAIL, but rarely why.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,800
MotionQA stores the decision with its
reason, score, thresholds and evidence.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:30,900
First, the live endpoint on AWS. CloudFront
serves the app from one EC2 Graviton instance.

8
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:34,600
Without a token, only the model status is visible.

9
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:39,800
The server reports the model ready
on OpenCV 5, and health is ok.

10
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:44,600
On October 16, twenty test
images ran through CloudFront.

11
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:49,800
All twenty decisions matched the local run.
Median inference took 450 milliseconds.

12
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:54,900
Every photo walks the same decision path.

13
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,800
Bad photos get RETAKE.
Doubtful parts go to a person.

14
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,400
Now a local demonstration, same model profile.

15
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:09,400
A good board scores 2.06,
below the PASS line at 2.16.

16
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,900
Bent pins push the score to
2.74, past the FAIL line.

17
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:21,200
A reviewer confirms. The machine
decision stays on record.

18
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:27,900
A blurred photo gets RETAKE,
and the session stays open.

19
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:34,600
The sharp retake passes. After three
failed tries, the part goes to a person.

20
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,900
This good board lands at
2.165, just over the PASS line.

21
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:44,500
So MotionQA asks a person instead of guessing.

22
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:50,900
Now a known failure. Test image 048
has a missing pin, and it passes.

23
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,600
The hottest spot sits on the
transducer, not on the missing pin.

24
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:01,300
Plain background looks normal to a
patch memory. This stays unfixed.

25
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:07,700
Board 043 lost both transducers. Its
identity distance, 0.155, falls in the gap.

26
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,800
An older policy called it NO_PART. Now
it goes to REVIEW, and stays in all 153.

27
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:19,600
Let us dissect one photo through OpenCV 5.

28
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:25,100
Otsu thresholding and contours find
the board. Sobel edges check focus.

29
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:30,600
The crop goes through MobileNetV2
on the new DNN engine.

30
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:36,600
Patch distances to normal boards form
the anomaly map and the evidence.

31
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:42,500
On AWS, the photo enters
through CloudFront and nginx.

32
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:48,200
FastAPI runs the pipeline on one t4g.small instance.

33
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:54,100
Evidence goes to S3, the record to
PostgreSQL, live events to Redis.

34
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:59,600
Secrets Manager holds the token.
CloudFormation built the stack.

35
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:05,600
Where does the data come from? The
public VisA archive on AWS Open Data.

36
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:11,100
804 good boards build the memory.
Validation images set the thresholds.

37
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:15,800
153 test images give the results.

38
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:21,400
Each dot is one test image,
placed by its anomaly score.

39
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:26,900
Two lines split the axis into PASS, REVIEW and FAIL.

40
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:32,600
1 of 53 defective boards passed.
4 of 100 good boards failed.

41
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:36,600
41 of 153 images went to REVIEW.

42
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:40,900
Image AUROC is 0.9745. It ranks
scores. It is not accuracy.

43
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:48,700
The OpenCV-only baseline: AUROC 0.8689, no
missed defects, 7 false rejections, 58 reviews.

44
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,900
These are exploratory development results.

45
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:59,700
Capture gates changed after test outcomes,
so this is not an independent evaluation.

46
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:06,700
The model covers this benchmark only. It
is not validated on other parts or lines.

47
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,800
About a third of good boards go
to REVIEW at this operating point.

48
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:18,900
A missing component on plain background
can pass. FAIL and REVIEW need a person.

49
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:25,600
Judges can open the CloudFront endpoint.
We share the operator token privately.

50
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:31,700
The public repository holds the code, the
evaluation files and this video's sources.

51
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,500
MotionQA, by team Kia Kiu. Thank you for watching.
